# Brainstorming Ideas Into Designs

> **原版全文见 `store/cache/brainstorming/SKILL.md`**（已拉取并登记在 registry，`mount: false`）。

## 上游要点（供将来合并时对照）

**三路径**（原版第 58–88 行）：
- **Spike** — 可行性问题，输出是答案不是代码；"No design doc, no spec file"，产物标 throwaway
- **Bounded** — 对**本仓库已有**代码的有界改动；"Understanding the kind of app is not enough —
  bounded means the flow you are changing is already here to read"；短方案要停下等明确 yes
- **Architectural** — 新项目/新子系统/改接口；完整流程到写规格 + `writing-plans` 交接

**棘轮**（第 86–88 行）："When in doubt between two paths, take the heavier one.
The ratchet is one-way: hidden complexity discovered mid-task upgrades the path — stop, say so,
and step up. Nothing downgrades mid-task."

**硬门控**（第 38–56 行）："A reply approves the stage actually presented. Approval of an idea or
feature scope does not approve artifacts that do not exist yet. Resume at the earliest incomplete
stage; do not turn one approval into permission to skip the rest of the selected path.
Read-only project exploration is allowed while those prerequisites remain incomplete."

**写回理解**（第 25–28 行）："Summarize the intended outcome, relevant constraints, and success
criteria in a short note your partner can assess. **Separate what they said from assumptions.**
Invite correction…"

**红旗表**（第 98–108 行，7 条）：核心是"为了省事贴标签本身就是疑点""bounded 衡量的是仓库不是熟悉度"
"spike 的产出是答案，留代码是新需求""每个任务各有各的分类和批准"。

**本 fork 的取舍**：砍掉 Visual Companion（第 268–285 行 + `scripts/` 6 个文件）、
规格文档落盘与 git 提交（第 237–266 行）、dot 流程图（第 140–182 行）、
`elements-of-style` / `writing-plans` 等具体 skill 交接（本机不需要）。
